iam Exshaw"] "’s yacht “Ollé” was the winner of both races in the 2-3 ton class, over 19 km (one long and two short rounds). In Race One, “Ollé” actually finished second to the French entry “Favorite”, but was the clear winner on adjusted time. Helmsman Exshaw lived in France and had two French crew members, making it a multi-national team. Second was the French “Favorite”, as only four yachts started in this class."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Prizes for Race One in this class were as follows: 1st – 600 francs; 2nd – 400 francs; 3rd – 250 francs; 4th – 100 francs; and 5th – 50 francs."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Adjusted Time"] [:th {} "Actual Time"] [:th {} "Handicap"] [:th {} "Weight"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Ollé"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "2-17:30"] [:td {} "1-47:48"] [:td {} "29:42"] [:td {} "2.10 tons"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/athletes/61957"} "William Exshaw"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61381"} "Frédéric Blanchy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62733"} "Jean le Vavasseur"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Favorite"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "2-20:03"] [:td {} "1-46:16"] [:td {} "33:47"] [:td {} "3.00 tons"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/athletes/63819"} "Léon Susse"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61865"} "Jacques Doucet"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/80371"} "Henri Mialaret"]